# 001 - Suspicious PowerShell Script Execution

## Alert Information

| Field | Details |
|---|---|
| Alert | Suspicious PowerShell Script Executed |
| Severity | Medium |
| Host | 172.16.17.206 |
| File | payload_1.ps1 |
| Platform | LetsDefend |

## Initial Analysis

A suspicious PowerShell script execution alert was generated.
The script was located in the user's Downloads directory.

## Investigation

### 1. File Analysis

The PowerShell payload was investigated using VirusTotal.

The sample was detected by multiple security vendors, indicating
that the file was potentially malicious.

### 2. Threat Intelligence

The investigation identified:

- Domain: kionagranada.com
- IP: 161.22.46.148
- Port: 443

### 3. SIEM / Firewall Investigation

Firewall logs were searched for communication involving the
affected host.

A connection was identified from:

Source:
172.16.17.206

Destination:
161.22.46.148:443

This confirmed communication between the affected host and the
identified malicious infrastructure.

## MITRE ATT&CK

- T1059.001 - PowerShell
